    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure why composing components would prevent spawn_local from working? It does have the limitations described in the docs, but should otherwise work. Do you have a repro?</p>",
        "id": 629272325,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Bratschi-Kaye (he)",
        "timestamp": 1791212291
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>here's a repro: <a href=\"https://github.com/dvc94ch/wac-repro\">https://github.com/dvc94ch/wac-repro</a><br>\nto build run ./build.sh, it hangs indefinitely because wit_bindgen::spawn_local is never polled</p>",
        "id": 629294533,
        "sender_full_name": "David Craven",
        "timestamp": 1791216260
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>my hypothesis for why it isn't possible is because wit-bindgen::block_on polls the tasks that were spawned in its memory using the <code>static mut TASKS</code>, and when composing the globals are isolated, so when the first component calls wit-bindgen::block_on it can't see the ones spawned in the other component</p>",
        "id": 629309831,
        "sender_full_name": "David Craven",
        "timestamp": 1791219920
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>but I'm not sure what the correct way of doing it is supposed to be</p>",
        "id": 629310071,
        "sender_full_name": "David Craven",
        "timestamp": 1791219979
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>never mind, decided that a microkernel is the wrong approach. with rust/cargo there isn't much point in splitting an OS into microservices or pushing them into user space anyway and the performance tax is real</p>",
        "id": 629506559,
        "sender_full_name": "David Craven",
        "timestamp": 1791284947
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the issue in your repro was that <code>write-via-stream</code> is sync lifted. So there's no way for it to keep running after it returns (only async lifts can do that).</p>",
        "id": 629524490,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Bratschi-Kaye (he)",
        "timestamp": 1791289147
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>have most of cli/random/clocks functional, should be able to get the rest working tomorrow.<br>\nexec 1<br>\nboot at 19:19:14 06.10.2026<br>\nrun 1<br>\nsend 1 Irq(8)<br>\nHello, world at 19:19:14<br>\nsuspend 1<br>\nrun 1<br>\nsend 1 Irq(8)<br>\nrandom bytes [196, 144, 86, 232, 59, 5, 210, 228, 71, 99, 123, 178, 119, 241, 179, 131, 50, 111, 166, 10, 15, 193, 229, 190, 227, 241, 151, 80, 91, 255, 236, 25]<br>\nsend 1 Irq(8)</p>\n<p>thread 'main' (1) panicked at app/src/main.rs:23:5:<br>\nlet's panic!<br>\nsend 1 Irq(8)<br>\nnote: run with <code>RUST_BACKTRACE=1</code> environment variable to display a backtrace<br>\nexit 1 with error UnreachableCodeReached</p>",
        "id": 629612646,
        "sender_full_name": "David Craven",
